        "Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Controls.SymbolIcon": {
            "comment": "The icon of the baseline set, and the one an application should reach for first: it already knows the font -- SymbolThemeFontFamily, the chain 'Segoe Fluent Icons,Segoe MDL2 Assets' -- so nothing but the glyph has to be said. WinRT names that glyph with the Symbol enumeration, and the synthetic member below lets FluentSymbol name it too.",
            "members": [
                "Symbol"
            ],
            "syntheticMembers": {
                "Symbol": {
                    "comment": "The same property, spelled with the other enumeration. Symbol names 197 glyphs, chosen for Windows 8 and living in the E1xx compatibility block; FluentSymbol names all 1533 the documentation of Segoe Fluent Icons carries, E700 and up. Both are code points in the font SymbolIcon already draws with, so this is one property with two vocabularies rather than two ways of doing a thing -- and it is why an icon whose name Symbol never had (QuietHours, Brightness) needs no FontIcon and no font name. The metadata declares one setter; this is the second overload of it, and the generator keeps both because it deduplicates on the signature.",
                    "cppType": "FluentSymbol",
                    "cppInclude": "FluentSymbol.h",
                    "function": "impl::set_fluent_symbol",
                    "include": "../impl/fluent_symbol.h"
                }
            }
        },
